 "result_text": "Pyflakes no longer crashes on `__all__, = (...)`. I ran it on your example and it exits cleanly with no output. The existing test suite still passes (714 passed, 44 skipped). I didn't add a test, as you asked.\n\nThe cause was in the binding code in `pyflakes/checker.py`. Pyflakes treated any module-level name `__all__` as an export list and passed the name's parent node to `ExportBinding`. For `__all__, = ...` that parent is a `Tuple`, which has no `.value`, hence the `AttributeError`.\n\nThe fix is to create an `ExportBinding` only when the parent is an `Assign`, `AugAssign` or `AnnAssign`. Any other form, such as the tuple-unpacking target, now gets an ordinary `Binding` instead.\n\nThis does not report the tuple form as invalid, which the issue suggested. It just stops pyflakes from crashing on it, and the names in the tuple are not checked as exports.",
